1	/**
2	 * @file
3	 *
4	 * @copyright
5	 * Copyright 2026 ISCAS.
6	 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
7	 *
8	 * @test @b sleef_neon
9	 * @parblock
10	 * Stress test for NEON data paths via SLEEF's vectorized transcendental
11	 * functions: the original sin/cos/exp/log families plus the u35
12	 * second-accuracy tier (sin/cos/log/exp2 — u35 has NO exp, exp2 is its
13	 * sibling with an independent polynomial chain) and the new asin/atan/
14	 * cbrt/log10/sinh/tanh/pow families, double & float, u10 and u35
15	 * accuracy, advsimd kernels. Long polynomial FMA dependency chains;
16	 * results only feed a byte-exact golden compare (data-flow payload:
17	 * faults surface as wrong values, not crashes — From Gates to SDCs
18	 * DATE'25). Pure functions => deterministic golden values computed once
19	 * in init with the same kernels. u10 and u35 are SLEEF's two INDEPENDENT
20	 * implementations of the same mathematics (different coefficients,
21	 * different FMA-chain schedules), so the second tier is a free
22	 * second-phase sample of the same silicon for the same math.
23	 * Covers the newest-instruction-generation risk area (PinDrop Obs12:
24	 * instructions fail most in their first arch gen) — the advsimd u10
25	 * codepaths are SLEEF's newest NEON implementations.
26	 *
27	 * The per-family element count is a runtime footprint knob:
28	 * "-O sleef_neon.nelems=N" (128..262144 in multiples of 4, default 1024;
29	 * the test-id prefix is required — a bare "nelems=N" is silently
30	 * ignored). It sweeps the replay working set across the cache hierarchy
31	 * (default 1024: a double segment's input+golden+scratch = 24KB stays
32	 * L1D-resident; 16384: ~384KB -> L2; 262144: 2MB per double buffer ->
33	 * LLC/DRAM; see the ELEMS_DEFAULT comment for the numbers), because
34	 * different cache structures hold different ACE residency. Omitting the
35	 * knob reproduces the historical compile-time ELEMS=1024 behavior
36	 * exactly: same RNG consumption order, byte-identical inputs/goldens.
37	 * @endparblock
38	 */
